    body: "Last updated: October 22, 2026\n\nThese Terms govern your use of edenbowls.com and the fresh dog food subscription offered by EZER ONE INC, doing business as Eden Bowls, based in Boca Raton, Florida (“Eden Bowls”, “we”, “us”). By creating an account or subscribing to a plan, you agree to these Terms and to our Privacy Policy.\n\n## 1. The service\n\nEden Bowls prepares fresh, frozen meals for dogs, sold by subscription. Based on the information you enter about your dog (breed, age, weight, activity level and dietary restrictions), the site calculates a suggested daily portion and builds a plan with a number of packs per delivery and the recipes you choose.\n\nOur recipes are formulated by a canine nutritionist. The suggested portion is an estimate based on the information you provide and is not a substitute for advice from a veterinarian. Dogs with medical conditions, allergies, pregnancy or special needs should have their diet reviewed by a veterinarian before you subscribe. Our products are labeled “for intermittent or supplemental feeding only”, as required by AAFCO. Please read the label.\n\nYou can adjust the number of packs in your plan manually on the My plan page. If you choose fewer packs than suggested, the site shows how much of the daily portion they cover, and the decision about supplementing your dog’s diet is yours. You are responsible for the accuracy of the information you enter about your dog.\n\n## 2. Your account\n\nYou must be 18 or older to subscribe. You will create an account with a valid email address, confirmed by a verification code. You are responsible for keeping your password confidential and for all activity under your account. Tell us right away if you suspect unauthorized use. We may suspend or close accounts used in violation of these Terms.\n\n## 3. Subscription, automatic renewal and billing\n\n**Automatic renewal and billing date.** Your subscription renews automatically. Deliveries follow the frequency you chose (weekly, every two weeks or monthly), and your card is charged once a month, on the same day of the month as your first charge (your billing date), for the deliveries scheduled for that month. Changing a delivery date does not change your billing date. Your subscription continues until you pause or cancel it. By subscribing, you authorize these recurring charges.\n\n**What you pay.** Your monthly charge is the price of the packs scheduled for that month, plus shipping and any applicable sales tax, as shown at checkout and on the My plan page. The price changes if you change your plan (recipes, number of packs or frequency), and the new price is shown on the My plan page before you save the change.\n\n**Price changes.** If we need to change prices, we will email you at least 30 days before the change takes effect. The new price applies only to charges made after that date, and you may cancel before then at no cost, including during the initial 3-month period.\n\n**Declined payments.** If a charge is declined, we will email you and put your delivery on hold. We will retry the charge over the next 7 days and remind you to update your card. If payment is not resolved within that time, the subscription is paused.\n\n**Receipts.** You receive an email confirmation and an invoice for every charge.\n\n## 4. Starter Box and initial 3-month period\n\n**Starter Box.** Your first box is the Starter Box, at 40% off. It contains meals for 10 days, in the amount calculated for your dog from the information you entered, plus a welcome booklet and a gift. The exact price is shown at checkout before you pay. The Starter Box discount is not sold separately: it is offered because it is tied to your subscription.\n\n**Initial 3-month period.** When you subscribe with the Starter Box, you agree to keep your subscription for 3 months, counted from your first charge. During this period you can pause, skip deliveries and change dates as usual, and those months still count toward the initial period.\n\n**Canceling before 3 months.** You can cancel at any time. If you cancel before completing the initial period, the Starter Box discount no longer applies and we will charge the difference between the regular Starter Box price and the amount you paid. This amount is shown on the My plan page before you confirm the cancellation. Example: if the regular Starter Box price is $100.00 and you paid $60.00 with the discount, the cancellation charge will be $40.00.\n\n**After 3 months.** Your subscription continues automatically, with no need to sign up again, and can be canceled at any time with no additional charge.\n\n## 5. Changing, skipping, pausing and canceling\n\nEach delivery has a change deadline, shown on the My plan page. Until that deadline, you can, at no cost:\n\n- skip the delivery, with no charge and no shipment for it;\n- move the delivery to another available date;\n- change recipes, number of packs or frequency;\n- pause or cancel your subscription.\n\nAfter the deadline, the order goes into production and that delivery can no longer be changed or canceled. Any changes apply to the following delivery.\n\nYou can cancel on the My plan page or by emailing hello@edenbowls.com. There is no cancellation fee. During the initial 3-month period, only the Starter Box rule in section 4 applies. Canceling online is as easy as signing up, and no phone call is required. When you pause, nothing is charged or shipped until you resume. When you cancel, there are no further charges, and if a paid cycle is already in production, that delivery is completed. Your plan settings are saved in case you want to reactivate.\n\n## 6. Shipping and delivery\n\nWe ship nationwide with UPS, in insulated packaging with the meals frozen. You provide the shipping address and are responsible for keeping it current and for someone being available to receive the package, or for indicating a safe place to leave it. We email the expected delivery date and a tracking number when your order ships.\n\nBecause the meals are perishable, deliveries cannot be rescheduled once the package has shipped, and we are not responsible for the condition of the meals after delivery to the address you provided. When your package arrives, check the packaging and put the meals in the freezer right away. To serve, thaw in the refrigerator and use within 3 days. Do not refreeze.\n\n## 7. Problems with an order, replacements and refunds\n\nIf your order arrives with damaged packaging, thawed, with a missing item or different from your plan, tell us within 24 hours of delivery at hello@edenbowls.com, with photos of the product and the packaging. In those cases we will resend the items or refund the corresponding amount, at your choice.\n\nBecause our meals are fresh, made to order and perishable, we do not accept returns for change of mind once an order has entered production. Refunds are issued to the original payment method within 10 business days after approval.\n\n## 8. Acceptable use and intellectual property\n\nYou agree to use the site only for lawful, personal purposes, not to attempt to access restricted areas, not to interfere with the operation of the system and not to copy site content for commercial use. All content (text, trademarks, logos, photographs, recipes and the portion calculator) belongs to Eden Bowls or its licensors and is protected by intellectual property law.\n\n## 9. Disclaimers and limitation of liability\n\nExcept as expressly stated in these Terms and to the extent permitted by law, the service and the site are provided “as is”. We are not liable for damages resulting from inaccurate information entered about your dog, improper storage after delivery, use of the meals contrary to the instructions, or your dog’s pre-existing health conditions. To the fullest extent permitted by law, our total liability to you for any claim arising from the service is limited to the amount you paid us in the 3 months before the claim. Some states do not allow certain limitations, so some of these may not apply to you. The site may be temporarily unavailable for maintenance, and we will give notice when possible.\n\n## 10. Communications\n\nBy subscribing, you agree to receive the emails needed to run your subscription (confirmations, shipping, billing, price change notices, pauses, cancellations and password resets). Marketing emails are sent only if you opt in and can be turned off through the link in every email.\n\n## 11. Changes to these Terms\n\nWe may update these Terms. We will notify you of material changes by email at least 15 days before they take effect. If you do not agree, you may cancel your subscription before the change takes effect. Continuing to use the service after that date means you accept the new version.\n\n## 12. Governing law and disputes\n\nThese Terms are governed by the laws of the State of Florida, without regard to its conflict of law rules. Any dispute will be resolved in the state or federal courts located in Palm Beach County, Florida, except that either party may bring an individual claim in small claims court. Nothing in these Terms limits any rights you have under the consumer protection laws of your state.\n\n## 13. Contact\n\nEZER ONE INC, doing business as Eden Bowls  \nBoca Raton, FL 33487, USA  \nCustomer care: hello@edenbowls.com\n"
